TAs Olivia and Hannah

Architecture
------------
40image.c       Provided main. Parses -c / -d and an optional filename,
                then calls compress40 or decompress40.

compress40.c    Implements compress40.h. Ties the steps together:
                  compress:   read PPM -> trim to even size -> convert
                              to component video -> pack each 2x2
                              block into a codeword -> write
                  decompress: read header -> read codewords -> unpack
                              each codeword into 4 pixels -> write PPM

images.c/.h     All image I/O. Reads PPMs and trims odd rows/columns;
                reads and writes the compressed header; reads and
                writes 32-bit codewords in big-endian order; creates
                the output pixmap (denominator 255).

conversions.c/.h
                Color-space conversion. RGB (scaled integers) to
                floating-point Y/Pb/Pr for compression, and Y/Pb/Pr
                back to RGB (clamped to [0, 1], then scaled) for
                decompression.

block.c/.h      2x2 block handling. chroma_conversion is mapped over a
                blocked array (blocksize 2) so it sees the four pixels
                of each block in a row; it averages Pb and Pr, runs the
                DCT, and hands the block to pack_codeword. Also holds
                the inverse DCT.

codeword.c/.h   Knows the codeword layout. Quantizes a (9 bits
                unsigned), b, c, d (5 bits signed, clamped to +/-0.3),
                and the chroma indices (4 bits each), and
                packs/unpacks them with Bitpack.

bitpack.c       Implements bitpack.h: fitsu/fitss, getu/gets,
                newu/news, and the Bitpack_Overflow exception.

uarray2.c/.h, uarray2b.c/.h, a2plain.c, a2blocked.c
                2D array and blocked 2D array implementations and their
                A2Methods suites, reused from the locality assignment.

ppmdiff.c       Testing tool. Prints the root mean square difference
                between two PPM images. Built with "make ppmdiff".


What has been implemented
-------------------------
To our knowledge, everything in the specification has been implemented
correctly, including both compression and decompression and the full
Bitpack interface.


